## RPG Character Builder

### Character Classes

Every RPG has classes that define your hero's role:

```xiom
enum CharacterClass {
  Warrior;
  Mage;
  Rogue;
}

fn class_description(cls: CharacterClass) -> Str {
  match cls {
    CharacterClass.Warrior => "Master of blade and shield",
    CharacterClass.Mage => "Wielder of arcane forces",
    CharacterClass.Rogue => "Shadow and subtlety incarnate",
  }
}
```

### Rolling Stats (Dice-Based)

Stats are rolled like real RPGs — d6 dice, 3 per stat, sum the results:

```xiom
fn roll_stat() -> Int {
  let d1 = random.range(1, 7);
  let d2 = random.range(1, 7);
  let d3 = random.range(1, 7);
  d1 + d2 + d3
}
```

### The Character Struct

```xiom
type Character {
  name: Str;
  class: CharacterClass;
  strength: Int;
  intelligence: Int;
  agility: Int;
  hit_points: Int;
  mana_points: Int;
  damage: Int;
  armor: Str;
  weapon: Str;
}
```

### Derived Stats

```xiom
fn calculate_hp(cls: CharacterClass, str: Int, agi: Int) -> Int {
  let base = match cls {
    CharacterClass.Warrior => 20,
    CharacterClass.Mage => 10,
    CharacterClass.Rogue => 14,
  };
  base + str * 2 + agi
}

fn calculate_mp(cls: CharacterClass, intel: Int) -> Int {
  let base = match cls {
    CharacterClass.Warrior => 4,
    CharacterClass.Mage => 25,
    CharacterClass.Rogue => 10,
  };
  base + intel * 3
}

fn calculate_damage(cls: CharacterClass, str: Int, intel: Int, agi: Int) -> Int {
  match cls {
    CharacterClass.Warrior => 5 + str * 2,
    CharacterClass.Mage => 3 + intel * 3,
    CharacterClass.Rogue => 4 + agi * 2 + str,
  }
}
```

### Equipment by Class

```xiom
fn get_equipment(cls: CharacterClass) -> (Str, Str) {
  match cls {
    CharacterClass.Warrior => ("Plate Armor", "Longsword"),
    CharacterClass.Mage => ("Arcane Robes", "Crystal Staff"),
    CharacterClass.Rogue => ("Leather Armor", "Twin Daggers"),
  }
}
```

